he inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x)?$"] ["question-f922b287-80df-5226-9ebc-4853a5adba77" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following:\n\n- The domain of a function $f(x)$ is the range of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the range of $f(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n-2<f(x)<4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n-2<x<4\n$$"] ["question-f922b287-80df-5226-9ebc-4853a5adba77" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-5385cd64-eaa0-5383-9862-ec961c5356f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5385cd64-eaa0-5383-9862-ec961c5356f1"] ["answer-9f173271-91e1-5ea2-b21f-c2beeb9aca0e" :answer/id #uuid "9f173271-91e1-5ea2-b21f-c2beeb9aca0e"] ["answer-9f173271-91e1-5ea2-b21f-c2beeb9aca0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9f173271-91e1-5ea2-b21f-c2beeb9aca0e" :answer/value "-2<x<4"] ["answer-d946bf11-11c9-5691-b17e-d17b5d30a9cf" :answer/id #uuid "d946bf11-11c9-5691-b17e-d17b5d30a9cf"] ["answer-d946bf11-11c9-5691-b17e-d17b5d30a9cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d946bf11-11c9-5691-b17e-d17b5d30a9cf" :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 4"] ["answer-f25f2f8c-33a3-5d70-9d04-894773be002f" :answer/id #uuid "f25f2f8c-33a3-5d70-9d04-894773be002f"] ["answer-f25f2f8c-33a3-5d70-9d04-894773be002f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f25f2f8c-33a3-5d70-9d04-894773be002f" :answer/value "-3<x<3"] ["answer-4c39f327-cff0-5908-a96b-7c4c25562bdd" :answer/id #uuid "4c39f327-cff0-5908-a96b-7c4c25562bdd"] ["answer-4c39f327-cff0-5908-a96b-7c4c25562bdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4c39f327-cff0-5908-a96b-7c4c25562bdd" :answer/value "-4\\le x<2"] ["answer-2fa1e24c-c035-562e-a8a2-07e26ba77f25" :answer/id #uuid "2fa1e24c-c035-562e-a8a2-07e26ba77f25"] ["answer-2fa1e24c-c035-562e-a8a2-07e26ba77f25" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2fa1e24c-c035-562e-a8a2-07e26ba77f25" :answer/value "-\\infty <x<\\infty "] ["answer-field-5385cd64-ea